WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.106
- He's an athlete,
actor, and entrepreneur.

00:00:03.106 --> 00:00:04.755
He's considered to be one of the greatest,

00:00:04.755 --> 00:00:07.455
if not the single
greatest basketball player

00:00:07.455 --> 00:00:08.479
of all time.

00:00:08.479 --> 00:00:10.304
He's worth over a billion dollars

00:00:10.304 --> 00:00:14.882
and his brand grosses over 2.25
billion dollars every year.

00:00:14.882 --> 00:00:16.043
He's Michael Jordan

00:00:16.043 --> 00:00:18.497
and here are his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:18.497 --> 00:00:21.247
(plane whooshes)

00:00:22.553 --> 00:00:24.185
- Every day, the first person there,

00:00:24.185 --> 00:00:25.086
before the sun,

00:00:25.086 --> 00:00:26.461
would be Jordan.

00:00:26.461 --> 00:00:28.668
And he was there because he wasn't good.

00:00:28.668 --> 00:00:31.303
He would work with a batting instructor

00:00:31.303 --> 00:00:32.496
and would work all day long

00:00:32.496 --> 00:00:37.054
and be the last person to
leave every night also.

00:00:37.054 --> 00:00:38.421
I asked him what it was
like for him in the morning

00:00:38.421 --> 00:00:40.696
and Jordan said "I get up
before the sun comes up,

00:00:40.696 --> 00:00:44.171
"and I make myself some
breakfast by myself,"

00:00:44.171 --> 00:00:46.108
he was down there alone.

00:00:46.108 --> 00:00:47.641
"And I get in the car

00:00:47.641 --> 00:00:50.787
"and I'm driving to Spring Training

00:00:50.787 --> 00:00:53.099
"and there is no one really
out on the roads yet.

00:00:53.099 --> 00:00:55.768
"And I look at the seat next to me,

00:00:55.768 --> 00:00:57.790
"and I see my dad,

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.373
"and I talk to him.

00:01:00.651 --> 00:01:01.722
"I think to myself,

00:01:01.722 --> 00:01:04.039
"Pops, we're doing this.

00:01:04.039 --> 00:01:05.995
"We're doing this together."

00:01:05.995 --> 00:01:07.765
(soft music)

00:01:07.765 --> 00:01:09.219
And the day would end

00:01:09.219 --> 00:01:11.067
and he would say to
the batting instructor,

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:12.108
"Can we do a little more.

00:01:12.108 --> 00:01:13.315
"I think I'm getting this.

00:01:13.315 --> 00:01:14.328
"I think I'm learning this.

00:01:14.328 --> 00:01:15.662
"I think I'm getting this"

00:01:15.662 --> 00:01:17.915
And that's when Sports
Illustrated put him on the cover

00:01:17.915 --> 00:01:21.773
saying that Michael Jordan
has embarrassed baseball.

00:01:21.773 --> 00:01:23.759
And as I would watch him there every night

00:01:23.759 --> 00:01:24.884
as the sun was going down

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.648
and the other ball players had left

00:01:26.648 --> 00:01:29.861
and I would see this guy
working to get better.

00:01:29.861 --> 00:01:31.654
Michael Jordan working to get better.

00:01:31.654 --> 00:01:32.804
I couldn't help thinking

00:01:32.804 --> 00:01:35.293
that if you ever have children,

00:01:35.293 --> 00:01:36.664
You ought to pray that they grow up

00:01:36.664 --> 00:01:38.432
someday to embarrass you like this.

00:01:38.432 --> 00:01:41.709
- I played professional
basketball for the Chicago Bulls.

00:01:41.709 --> 00:01:43.341
(frenetic violin music)

00:01:43.341 --> 00:01:44.771
- [Announcer] 32 seconds to go.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:47.540
A one point lead for Georgetown.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.123
Daugherty to Black.

00:01:50.148 --> 00:01:51.858
The time 18.

00:01:51.858 --> 00:01:54.648
Shot, Jordan, Michael Jordan!

00:01:54.648 --> 00:01:57.447
- If I had to trace my evolution,

00:01:57.447 --> 00:01:59.162
the Michael Jordan evolution,

00:01:59.162 --> 00:02:00.643
it'd always have to start back in college

00:02:00.643 --> 00:02:03.801
hitting the shot against
Georgetown in 1982

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:06.375
when I really didn't know
exactly what I was doing.

00:02:06.375 --> 00:02:08.402
- [Announcer] North Carolina has won

00:02:08.402 --> 00:02:10.652
the 1982 NCAA championship.

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:14.785
- It awakened a person inside of me

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:16.992
to excel,

00:02:16.992 --> 00:02:17.953
to compete to excel,

00:02:17.953 --> 00:02:21.181
to be one of the best, or be the best.

00:02:21.181 --> 00:02:22.832
That drove me.

00:02:22.832 --> 00:02:24.408
And I guess with that shot

00:02:24.408 --> 00:02:26.328
it kind of ignited a fire inside of me

00:02:26.328 --> 00:02:28.615
that nothing was going to stop.

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:31.485
- [Announcer] Jordan down
the middle all the way!

00:02:31.485 --> 00:02:34.200
- [Announcer] Jordan to the hoop!

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:38.576
- [Announcer] Jordan down
the lane all the way!

00:02:38.576 --> 00:02:40.871
- [Announcer] - Jordan,
who has it on the break,

00:02:40.871 --> 00:02:42.424
driving all the way in!

00:02:42.424 --> 00:02:45.507
(yelling and cheers)

00:02:46.724 --> 00:02:48.655
- I wanted to excel my game

00:02:48.655 --> 00:02:51.945
and isolate my game from everybody else.

00:02:51.945 --> 00:02:54.999
That I was more than
just, a few dimensional.

00:02:54.999 --> 00:02:56.568
Even when it came to Magic Johnson.

00:02:56.568 --> 00:02:59.639
I mean, Magic Johnson was a crowd pleaser.

00:02:59.639 --> 00:03:01.311
He was a good offensive player.

00:03:01.311 --> 00:03:02.347
He was a great motivator.

00:03:02.347 --> 00:03:04.410
Average defensive player.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.316
I wanted to change that.

00:03:06.316 --> 00:03:07.451
I wanted to take it another step.

00:03:07.451 --> 00:03:08.396
I wanted to do all those things

00:03:08.396 --> 00:03:11.623
that could separate me from Magic Johnson.

00:03:11.623 --> 00:03:13.286
I'm not saying he wasn't great.

00:03:13.286 --> 00:03:14.598
He still is great.

00:03:14.598 --> 00:03:17.324
But we're are great in
our own different way.

00:03:17.324 --> 00:03:20.172
And that was motivational for me.

00:03:20.172 --> 00:03:22.616
And to this day it still is.

00:03:22.616 --> 00:03:25.116
(funky music)

00:03:26.062 --> 00:03:29.729
I missed more than 9,000
shots in my career.

00:03:31.525 --> 00:03:33.775
I've lost almost 300 games.

00:03:35.729 --> 00:03:39.896
26 times I have been trusted
to take the game winning shot

00:03:40.888 --> 00:03:41.805
and missed.

00:03:43.717 --> 00:03:47.884
I've failed over, and over,
and over again in my life.

00:03:49.197 --> 00:03:51.076
And that is why

00:03:51.076 --> 00:03:52.530
I succeed.

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:56.004
I never feel that I am at my best.

00:03:56.004 --> 00:03:58.507
I feel I still have room to improve.

00:03:58.507 --> 00:04:02.236
I still set goals for
myself to strive for.

00:04:02.236 --> 00:04:05.931
I'm never complacent
with what I've achieved

00:04:05.931 --> 00:04:08.554
even though it's been
very successful for me.

00:04:08.554 --> 00:04:09.978
I still feel I have a lot to prove

00:04:09.978 --> 00:04:14.198
not just as a player but
as a person, as a father,

00:04:14.198 --> 00:04:17.051
to some extent as a role model,

00:04:17.051 --> 00:04:18.301
in all aspects.

00:04:20.049 --> 00:04:24.658
So I'm never really too
complacent with myself

00:04:24.658 --> 00:04:26.282
or with what I've achieved.

00:04:26.282 --> 00:04:27.688
When I get to a point where I feel

00:04:27.688 --> 00:04:29.518
I can't improve as a player,

00:04:29.518 --> 00:04:30.911
I walk away from the game.

00:04:30.911 --> 00:04:33.764
I still feel that I have a plateau

00:04:33.764 --> 00:04:36.067
that I haven't reached yet,

00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:40.830
in terms of my skills or
my expectations of myself.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:42.376
I'm always going to expect myself to do

00:04:42.376 --> 00:04:46.221
certain things, or surpass certain things.

00:04:46.221 --> 00:04:47.823
As long as I believe that then

00:04:47.823 --> 00:04:51.990
my road to success is going
to continue to expand.

00:04:52.974 --> 00:04:55.435
Sports is a tool that teaches.

00:04:55.435 --> 00:04:57.148
It teaches you bad things.

00:04:57.148 --> 00:04:58.908
I can also teach you good things.

00:04:58.908 --> 00:05:00.871
It's how you perceive those things.

00:05:00.871 --> 00:05:02.453
I've looked at every experience

00:05:02.453 --> 00:05:04.224
that I've had, negative and positive

00:05:04.224 --> 00:05:06.017
and taken that as a positive.

00:05:06.017 --> 00:05:07.595
I wouldn't change anything

00:05:07.595 --> 00:05:08.909
because I think it would alter

00:05:08.909 --> 00:05:10.385
some of the other things that happened.

00:05:10.385 --> 00:05:12.281
So When I look back, I can't say that

00:05:12.281 --> 00:05:14.621
I've had any bad things happen.

00:05:14.621 --> 00:05:16.461
Sure, you don't want bad things to happen

00:05:16.461 --> 00:05:17.556
but you deal with bad things.

00:05:17.556 --> 00:05:19.634
You can't have good without bad.

00:05:19.634 --> 00:05:21.717
It's not about the shoes.

00:05:23.014 --> 00:05:26.181
(inspirational music)

00:05:27.917 --> 00:05:30.844
It's about knowing where you are going.

00:05:30.844 --> 00:05:33.594
Not forgetting where you started.

00:05:38.004 --> 00:05:41.171
It's about having the courage to fail.

00:05:43.286 --> 00:05:46.867
Not breaking, when you are broken.

00:05:46.867 --> 00:05:49.620
Taking everything you've been given

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.953
and making something better.

00:05:54.475 --> 00:05:56.111
It's about work

00:05:56.111 --> 00:05:57.194
before glory,

00:06:00.811 --> 00:06:02.894
and what's inside of you.

00:06:03.846 --> 00:06:07.427
It's doing what they say you can't.

00:06:07.427 --> 00:06:09.649
It's not about the shoes.

00:06:09.649 --> 00:06:12.675
It's about what you do in them.

00:06:12.675 --> 00:06:14.117
It's about being

00:06:14.117 --> 00:06:16.117
who you were born to be.

00:06:17.513 --> 00:06:19.312
You know, we're all old.

00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:21.572
And sure, we're tired,
it's been a long season.

00:06:21.572 --> 00:06:24.072
But mentally we have a vision,

00:06:26.051 --> 00:06:29.384
we have a finish that we have to obtain.

00:06:30.453 --> 00:06:31.663
Sometimes you have to do it

00:06:31.663 --> 00:06:34.246
when you're old and you're tired.

00:06:34.246 --> 00:06:37.913
I think it is a test
of your will to succeed

00:06:39.521 --> 00:06:42.890
when you have to deal with
some of these negatives.

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:46.151
And I'm pretty sure by
the end of this play-off,

00:06:46.151 --> 00:06:48.351
you will see the old and the tired people,

00:06:48.351 --> 00:06:51.610
we're very, very young
and strong mentally.

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:54.420
Maybe it's my own fault.

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:56.752
Maybe I led you to believe it was easy

00:06:56.752 --> 00:06:58.709
when it wasn't.

00:06:58.709 --> 00:07:00.887
Maybe I made you think
my highlights started

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:02.359
at the free-throw line

00:07:02.359 --> 00:07:04.045
and not in the gym.

00:07:04.045 --> 00:07:06.905
Maybe I made you think
that every shot I took

00:07:06.905 --> 00:07:08.405
was a game winner.

00:07:10.948 --> 00:07:12.920
That my game was built on flash

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:14.003
and not fire.

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:16.545
(dramatic music)

00:07:16.545 --> 00:07:18.093
Maybe it's my fault that you didn't see

00:07:18.093 --> 00:07:20.012
that failure gave me strength,

00:07:20.012 --> 00:07:22.595
that my pain was my motivation.

00:07:23.947 --> 00:07:26.264
Maybe I led you to believe that basketball

00:07:26.264 --> 00:07:29.658
was a god given gift and
not something I worked for

00:07:29.658 --> 00:07:31.991
every single day of my life.

00:07:34.797 --> 00:07:37.047
Maybe I destroyed the game.

00:07:41.728 --> 00:07:44.728
Or maybe you're just making excuses.

00:07:46.329 --> 00:07:48.230
- [Announcer] The Bulls
can win it right here.

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:49.511
The Bulls can win it.

00:07:49.511 --> 00:07:50.715
Unbelievable!

00:07:50.715 --> 00:07:52.166
13 seconds left.

00:07:52.166 --> 00:07:53.356
Jordan left side.

00:07:53.356 --> 00:07:55.046
- I practice as if I'm playing in the game

00:07:55.046 --> 00:07:57.426
so when the moment comes in the game.

00:07:57.426 --> 00:07:58.665
It's not new to me.

00:07:58.665 --> 00:08:00.888
That's the beauty of
the game of basketball.

00:08:00.888 --> 00:08:02.510
That's the reason why you practice.

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:03.527
That's the effort.

00:08:03.527 --> 00:08:04.649
So when you get to that moment,

00:08:04.649 --> 00:08:05.605
you don't have to think.

00:08:05.605 --> 00:08:07.613
Instinctively, things happen.

00:08:07.613 --> 00:08:09.190
- [Announcer] Jordan drives.

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:11.940
(dramatic music)

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:15.163
And fires, yeah!

00:08:16.087 --> 00:08:17.837
The bulls lead 87-86!

00:08:19.801 --> 00:08:22.301
Michael Jordan with 45 points.

00:08:26.963 --> 00:08:30.309
- You know, I think there
was a very defining moment

00:08:30.309 --> 00:08:32.907
of what my career was in Chicago.

00:08:32.907 --> 00:08:34.932
- [Announcer] The Chicago Bulls have won

00:08:34.932 --> 00:08:37.349
their sixth NBA championship.

00:08:42.712 --> 00:08:45.825
- [Announcer] If that's the
last image of Michael Jordan,

00:08:45.825 --> 00:08:48.165
how magnificent is it?

00:08:48.165 --> 00:08:48.998
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:08:48.998 --> 00:08:52.341
I made this video because
Reynado asked me to,

00:08:52.341 --> 00:08:53.923
so if there is a famous entrepreneur

00:08:53.923 --> 00:08:55.221
that you want me to profile next,

00:08:55.221 --> 00:08:56.533
leave it in the comments below

00:08:56.533 --> 00:08:57.797
and I will see what I can do.

00:08:57.797 --> 00:08:59.379
I'd also love to know which of

00:08:59.379 --> 00:09:02.099
Jordan's top 10 rules you like the most.

00:09:02.099 --> 00:09:03.514
Let me know in the comments.

00:09:03.514 --> 00:09:04.808
I'm going to join the discussion.

00:09:04.808 --> 00:09:06.068
Thank you for watching.

00:09:06.068 --> 00:09:07.364
Continue to believe

00:09:07.364 --> 00:09:09.197
and I'll see you soon.

